10. ANALYTICS STACK

Evaluate the current Python standard-library-only analytical implementation.

I specifically want the engine to become capable of more sophisticated statistical analysis.

Evaluate and introduce libraries where they provide genuine analytical value:

Pandas

For:

* historical time series
* grouping
* resampling
* rolling windows
* feature engineering
* historical aggregation

NumPy

For:

* numerical operations
* vectorized calculations
* statistical features
* normalization
* numerical anomaly scoring

SciPy

Use selectively where statistically meaningful:

* statistical tests
* distributions
* outlier analysis
* signal/time-series analysis
* other appropriate statistical methods

scikit-learn

Evaluate whether it should be introduced for:

* Isolation Forest
* clustering
* anomaly detection
* feature scaling
* dimensionality reduction where useful
* other appropriate unsupervised methods

Do NOT add libraries simply to increase the dependency list.

For every new library, document:

problem → method → why this library → why simpler methods are insufficient

